From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 11:28:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pcie: mediatek-gen3: add link-up settle delay

On MT7988A the LTSSM occasionally fails to progress out of
detect.quiet within the PCI_PM_D3COLD_WAIT (100ms) poll window
after the final PCIE_PE_RSTB deassert, and probe fails with
-ETIMEDOUT. A short settling delay between the last
writel_relaxed() and the link poll is enough to let the RC start
receiver detection reliably. Symptom was discovered on
SDG-8713v (MT7988A + MT7992/MT7996) with the wifi-reset GPIO
flow active. Adding a ~1ms settle window fixes the race.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek-gen3.c |    8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek-gen3.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek-gen3.c
@@ -510,6 +510,14 @@ static int mtk_pcie_startup_port(struct
 		writel_relaxed(val, pcie->base + PCIE_RST_CTRL_REG);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Let the RC settle after the final reset-register write before
+	 * polling the link. Without this short delay the LTSSM occasionally
+	 * stays wedged at detect.quiet for longer than PCI_PM_D3COLD_WAIT on
+	 * MT7988A, and probe times out with -ETIMEDOUT.
+	 */
+	usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+
 	/* Check if the link is up or not */
 	err = readl_poll_timeout(pcie->base + PCIE_LINK_STATUS_REG, val,
 				 !!(val & PCIE_PORT_LINKUP), 20,
